  "an \`allowFormattingRules\` rule this package keeps on": "throws: @gpahal/eslint-config: \`allowFormattingRules\`: \`no-unexpected-multiline\`: stays on already; this package keeps it on",
  "an absolute \`gitignore.files\` path": "throws: @gpahal/eslint-config: \`gitignore.files\`: path \`/abs\` is absolute. Make it relative to \`root\`",
  "an absolute \`nextjs.rootDir\`": "throws: @gpahal/eslint-config: \`nextjs.rootDir\`: path \`/apps/web\` is absolute. Make it relative to \`root\`",
  "an absolute \`typeAware.ignores\` glob": "throws: @gpahal/eslint-config: \`typeAware.ignores\`: glob \`/abs/**\` starts with \`/\`, but globs are relative to \`root\`. Write \`abs/**\`",
  "an absolute glob in an \`.override()\` of a split config of yours": "rejects: @gpahal/eslint-config: \`.override('user/split')\`: \`files\`: glob \`<fixtures>/rules/src/**\` starts with \`/\`, but globs are relative to \`root\`. Write \`src/**\`",
  "an array as the options": "throws: @gpahal/eslint-config: options: expected an object of options, received an array",
  "an empty \`vitest.files\`": "throws: @gpahal/eslint-config: \`vitest.files\`: lists no globs, so it would match no file. Leave it out for the default",
  "an empty glob": "throws: @gpahal/eslint-config: \`testFiles\`: glob \`\` is empty",
  "an unknown \`typescript.exhaustiveSwitch\`": "throws: @gpahal/eslint-config: \`typescript.exhaustiveSwitch\`: expected \`"default"\` or \`"strict"\`, received \`"all"\`",
  "an unknown option": "throws: @gpahal/eslint-config: \`typescript.typeAwre\`: unknown option. Known options: \`rules\`, \`rulesTypeAware\`, \`library\`, \`exhaustiveSwitch\`, \`strictBooleanExpressions\`",
  "another plugin under a preset plugin name, in a nested config of yours": "rejects: @gpahal/eslint-config: \`configs[0][1].plugins\`: registers \`package-json\` again with a different plugin. Set its rules with \`packageJson.rules\` instead",
  "another plugin under the \`@gpahal\` name": "rejects: @gpahal/eslint-config: \`configs[0].plugins\`: registers \`@gpahal\` again with a different plugin. Remove it from the config",
  "brace alternatives of no code file": "throws: @gpahal/eslint-config: \`testFiles\`: glob \`src/{a.css,{b,c}/d.css}\` matches no JavaScript or TypeScript file. End it in \`*\` or an extension of one, as in \`**/*.ts\`",
  "formatting rules that a config of yours extends": "throws: @gpahal/eslint-config: \`configs[0]\` (\`user/configs[0] > ExtendedConfig[0]\`): 2 issues
  \`curly\`: is a rule that eslint-config-prettier turns off, since it conflicts with Prettier or is only safe with some options
  \`semi\`: is a rule that eslint-config-prettier turns off, since it conflicts with Prettier or is only safe with some options
A plugin's preset that the config is or extends may turn on such rules: wrap it in \`withoutFormattingRules\`. Turn them off, or list them in \`allowFormattingRules\`",
  "no \`tailwindcss.entryPoint\`": "throws: @gpahal/eslint-config: \`tailwindcss.entryPoint\`: expected an absolute path or one relative to \`root\`, or a \`file:\` URL or URL string with an absolute path, such as \`import.meta.resolve('./src/styles/global.css')\`, received \`undefined\`. Set it, as in \`{ entryPoint: 'src/styles.css' }\`",
  "only negated globs in \`node.scope\`": "throws: @gpahal/eslint-config: \`node.scope\`: lists only negated globs, so it would match no file. Add the globs of the files to match, as in \`['src/**', '!src/legacy/**']\`",
  "only negated globs in \`server.files\`": "throws: @gpahal/eslint-config: \`server.files\`: lists only negated globs, so it would match no file. Add the globs of the files to match, as in \`['src/**', '!src/legacy/**']\`",
  "only negated globs in \`testFiles\`": "throws: @gpahal/eslint-config: \`testFiles\`: lists only negated globs, so it would match no file. Add the globs of the files to match, as in \`['src/**', '!src/legacy/**']\`",
  "the \`astro\` preset plugin's layout rule": "throws: @gpahal/eslint-config: \`astro.rules\`: \`astro/semi\`: is a layout rule for files that Prettier formats, so it conflicts with Prettier or is only safe with some options. Turn it off, or list it in \`allowFormattingRules\`",
  "the \`html\` preset plugin's layout rule": "throws: @gpahal/eslint-config: \`html.rules\`: \`@html-eslint/indent\`: is a layout rule for files that Prettier formats, so it conflicts with Prettier or is only safe with some options. Turn it off, or list it in \`allowFormattingRules\`",
  "the project service in a config of yours": "throws: @gpahal/eslint-config: \`configs[0]\`: \`languageOptions.parserOptions.projectService\`: is set from \`root\` and \`typeAware\`, so a config of yours may not change it. List the files to lint with the default project in \`typeAware.allowDefaultProject\`, or those to lint without type information in \`typeAware.ignores\`",
  "too many brace alternatives": "throws: @gpahal/eslint-config: \`node.scope\`: glob \`src/{1..5000}.ts\` expands to more than 1000 globs. List fewer alternatives",
}
`;
